		{"id":"67323c89cca482a7","type":"text","text":"# crontab\n\nSchedule commands to execute, in 2 days, every hour, or every sunday","x":-60,"y":-620,"width":280,"height":170},
		{"id":"1cbbc2e99650ddde","type":"text","text":"# awk\nText processing language\nReads a file per line, divide the line by column accesible by calling vars $1, $2, $3 etc.\n\n``` bash\nawk '<pattern> {<action>;<action>;...}'\n```\n\n## Arrays\n``` bash \n# Arrays are created automatically, where you are\n# asked to place an array, just place the name you want\n# to assign to it\n\nBEGIN {\n\t# no array initialisation\n    a[1] = 42\n    a[2] = 99\n\n    print a[1] # 42\n}\n```\n\n``` bash\n# Calling a function 'split', which needs an array,\n# we just pass 'a' and it will create it automatically\nawk '{split($1, a, \"/\"); print(a[1])}' ./file\n```\n\n\n\n","x":-1140,"y":120,"width":640,"height":740}
